  "scope": "Separate original collection authoring/visible TagList phases; complete list render state/ref/style/context and empty-state focus observations; native root/list typography; depth-first logical rows and shared actual selection-indicator state. Full TagGroup contexts/input/AT, maintained/public/consumer/native/profile acceptance remain required. Owning field IDs compose explicit and referenced labels through the pinned useField/useLabels contract; native resolvers read the original raw own label for self references. Actual visible field-slot name/description/error host bindings, native text refs, grouped remove Button slots and current multi-target keyboard admission; owner scene retains veto/echo and real virtualization. The Button-only slot extension is omitted from existing ToggleButton and grouped-row props to preserve their prior type boundaries. Exact-source proof confirms TagGroupInner deliberately strips the virtual-focus collection-context flag and retains physical item focus; the existing native policy matches it. Grouped custom render forwards complete state/original props and actual native refs, including replacement retirement; initial autofocus preserves native admission and window/input lifetimes. A private native Tab-stop field separates relative eligibility from programmatic focus for grouped rows, including the all-disabled autofocus source outcome. The maintained scene requests read-only SDK accessibility snapshots through actual outer/list/item refs, receiving original packets only from the current live owner/target. Chunked native logs retain SDK collection positions/counts without business-state injection or public inspection APIs.",
